; stashremote.eval - an edit of a BROWSED level stashes only the layer it
; changes (code-review C307). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 31, on a
; scratch copy of dungeon-demo; the party stays on eval_arena throughout.
;
; 1. AN ERASE OF NOTHING at 4,1 on crypt2, which holds no stash yet - refused,
;    and stashing neither layer. It climbs the whole ladder - a stair, a record,
;    a prop or fixture, the square's looks - each tried on a copy of the level
;    as it reads (it used to stash both layers up front). First, so that no
;    stash a later edit made can stand in for one this made.
; 2. A WALL PAINTED on crypt2 at 3,1, a square nothing stands on. The paint
;    changes the map; it used to stash crypt2's .ent as well (the prune that
;    buries what stood on a painted square created the stash before looking),
;    so the save rewrote an .ent nobody had changed.
; 3. AN ITEM ERASED on crypt1 at 12,1: the .ent changes and the map does not,
;    so crypt1's .ent is written and its .map is not - every .ent stash used to
;    bring a map stash with it.
; EditorTest reads the files: crypt2.ent and crypt1.map byte for byte as the
; copy was made; crypt2.map walled at 3,1; crypt1.ent without the potion.

logecho on
reset
editor
levels view crypt2
expect-refuse editor erase 4 1
echo --- empty erase ---
stashes
editor drag walls wall_marble 3 1
echo --- painted ---
stashes
levels view crypt1
editor erase 12 1
echo --- item erase ---
stashes
savemap
echo --- end ---
